WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:07.450
He's been riddled with bullets, set ablaze,
electrocuted, and even injected with corrosives,

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:12.589
so you didn't really think that a flaming
basement would be Michael Myers' coffin now,

00:00:12.589 --> 00:00:13.589
did you?

00:00:13.589 --> 00:00:15.999
Here's the ending of "Halloween Kills," explained.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:22.880
During the conclusion of 2018's "Halloween,"
the Shape was last seen trapped in the burning

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:30.000
basement of Laurie Strode's compound — a
fiery snare the tactical heroine devised herself.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.630
As a severely wounded Laurie, daughter Karen,
and granddaughter Allyson all fled to safety,

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:40.380
they flagged down a passing truck and escaped
into town.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:44.570
We then cut back to the basement ... and saw
no sign of Michael.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:47.580
It's here where "Halloween Kills" picks up.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.260
"No no no!

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:50.940
Let it burn!

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.620
Let it burn!"

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.660
Meanwhile, back at the compound, firefighters
unwittingly free Michael from his pit of flames,

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:01.100
and there's no gratitude from the guy whatsoever.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:06.400
He thanks his rescuers by immediately dispatching
them in brutal fashion.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:11.970
In this very first scene, it's immediately
clear that writer-director David Gordon Green

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.799
isn't playing around.

00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:19.890
This is Michael Myers dialed up to 11, and
he goes on to slay dozens of Haddonfield residents

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:24.299
with a fury we've never seen before — and
the camera never shies away.

00:01:25.299 --> 00:01:30.760
The story of "Halloween Kills" is simple:
Michael goes on a murderous rampage as Haddonfield

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:36.290
residents band together to hunt him down while
Laurie recovers in the hospital.

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:41.490
It all leads up to a bloody battle royale
between Michael and an angry mob.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:46.799
As Laurie is rushed to the hospital, we cut
to a local Haddonfield bar filled with residents

00:01:46.799 --> 00:01:51.170
who are not yet aware of what went down at
the Strode homestead.

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:57.259
During a memorial ceremony, we're reintroduced
to three characters from the 1978 movie: Marion

00:01:57.259 --> 00:02:03.409
Chambers, who survived an attack when Michael
first escaped Smith's Grove Sanitarium, and

00:02:03.409 --> 00:02:09.030
Lindsey Wallace and Tommy Doyle, the two kids
Laurie was babysitting on Halloween night.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:14.140
Tommy takes to the stage and tells the traumatic
story of his encounter with Michael Myers.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:19.380
It's evident that he is suffering from PTSD,
so when the news breaks that Laurie was attacked

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:25.260
at her compound and photos of a crashed Smith's
Grove sanitarium bus flash on the television

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:30.200
screen, this immediately triggers him to go
into full-on vigilante mode.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:35.980
Armed with a bat provided by the bartender,
he quickly stirs up an angry mob, who've decided

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:39.980
they will take the law into their own hands
and hunt down Michael themselves.

00:02:41.599 --> 00:02:47.380
Meanwhile, back at the hospital, we're reintroduced
to former town sheriff Brackett, who now works

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:49.550
as a hospital security officer.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:54.140
In the original movie, he was also the father
of Laurie's best friend Annie.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:58.819
She was also one of Michael's victims, so
much like Tommy and the rest of the riled-up

00:02:58.819 --> 00:03:01.989
mob, Brackett wants some good old-fashioned
revenge.

00:03:01.989 --> 00:03:05.090
"When he gets here, I'm going to kill him.

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:08.560
Because 40 years ago when I was a kid, you
protected me."

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:13.200
While Laurie is sedated and recovering at
the hospital, Karen and Allyson learn that

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.090
Michael is still at large.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:19.780
When Allyson learns that her boyfriend Cameron
and his father Lonnie are joining in on the

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:24.340
hunt for Myers, she signs up, much against
her mother's wishes.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:29.650
After all, Michael did kill her father in
the previous film, so as you can see, everyone

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:31.460
wants in on the action.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:38.090
Fun fact: Lonnie is a lesser-known character
who was only in a few scenes in the 1978 original.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:42.800
One of Tommy's bullies, he was also the kid
being dared to enter the Myers house.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.570
"Lonnie, get your ass away from there!"

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:53.340
During the final act, Lonnie takes a look
at a town map and realizes that Michael's

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:59.100
blood trail points directly to his childhood
home, the Myers house, which is now occupied

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:04.000
by a couple, Big John and Little John, who
unfortunately have already met their end at

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.910
the hands of you know who.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:11.239
As Cameron, Allyson and Lonnie drive up to
the house, Lonnie decides to have a look-see

00:04:11.239 --> 00:04:14.799
and makes the ill-advised choice of going
in alone.

00:04:14.799 --> 00:04:19.999
After a blaring gunshot is heard, Cameron
and Allyson rush in, only to discover yet

00:04:19.999 --> 00:04:21.529
another bloodbath.

00:04:21.529 --> 00:04:26.330
After they discover the bodies of Big John,
Little John, and Lonnie, Michael appears and

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:31.199
takes out Cameron by repeatedly bludgeoning
him against the banister.

00:04:31.199 --> 00:04:36.150
During the bone-crushing struggle, he then
sets his gaze on Allyson, who suffers a fall

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:37.800
down the staircase.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:43.889
As Michael readies to plunge his knife, Allyson
fearlessly screams, "Do it!" just as he is

00:04:43.889 --> 00:04:46.520
pierced from behind by a pitchfork.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:49.580
Surprise, it's momma Karen to the rescue.

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:54.152
While Michael is fazed by the sneak attack,
she takes off his mask and taunts him with

00:04:54.152 --> 00:04:55.152
it.

00:04:55.152 --> 00:04:56.152
"Come and get it!"

00:04:56.152 --> 00:05:01.139
As Michael pursues Karen behind the Myers
house, he's lured to a quiet empty street

00:05:01.139 --> 00:05:04.520
with nothing but his mask laying in the middle
of the road.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:05.520
It's a trap!

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:11.330
As he goes to reclaim it, the angry mob emerges,
which includes Tommy and Brackett and numerous

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:13.110
armed local residents.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:17.849
It's here Michael is met with some hardcore
Haddonfield justice.

00:05:17.849 --> 00:05:22.229
Michael is riddled with bullets and stabbed
multiple times while Tommy gets to put his

00:05:22.229 --> 00:05:25.870
rage and trusty bat to full-throttle use.

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:27.809
Even Karen gets in on the action.

00:05:27.809 --> 00:05:31.650
Grabbing a knife, she delivers the final blow
— or is it?

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:36.340
Unfortunately, the mob lets their guard down
and thinks it's over.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:40.659
As Karen heads back to the Myers house to
check on her daughter, Michael springs to

00:05:40.659 --> 00:05:45.089
his feet and takes everyone out, including
Tommy and Brackett.

00:05:45.089 --> 00:05:50.249
Back at the Myers house, Karen gazes out the
very same window Michael once did, unaware

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:52.419
of the carnage taking place outside.

00:05:52.419 --> 00:05:58.619
Soon, the victorious Shape emerges from behind
her and does what he does best.

00:05:58.619 --> 00:06:01.770
Karen's lifeless body drops to the floor.

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:02.770
Could she be alive?

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:05.689
It's doubtful, but you never know with these
movies.

00:06:05.689 --> 00:06:08.999
But her lifeless eyes most likely spell death.

00:06:08.999 --> 00:06:14.050
The ending of "Halloween Kills" is the polar
opposite of the previous film's conclusion.

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:19.179
As we learned in 2018's "Halloween," Karen
had a strained relationship with her mother.

00:06:19.179 --> 00:06:24.259
She resented Laurie and pegged her as a crazy
alcoholic who spent her entire life obsessing

00:06:24.259 --> 00:06:28.270
over some "boogeyman" who randomly attacked
her on a Halloween night.

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:33.369
But she ultimately learned that the boogeyman
was indeed real, and her mother was only preparing

00:06:33.369 --> 00:06:34.369
her.

00:06:34.369 --> 00:06:38.909
It may have taken a horrific event to bring
them together, but Laurie seemingly vanquished

00:06:38.909 --> 00:06:44.610
her nemesis and she did it side by side with
her daughter, ultimately gaining her back.

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:48.901
She succeeded at protecting her family from
the evil she knew would one day return.

00:06:48.901 --> 00:06:50.839
In her eyes, she won.

00:06:50.839 --> 00:06:54.449
But as we learn in "Halloween Kills," that
victory was short-lived.

00:06:54.449 --> 00:07:00.770
Karen's demise sets the stage for what could
be the darkest, most revenge-fueled "Halloween"

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:01.770
movie yet.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:06.189
Losing her only child may very well push Laurie
Strode to the brink of madness.

00:07:06.189 --> 00:07:09.949
Will she torture herself for not being able
to protect her daughter from the one thing

00:07:09.949 --> 00:07:11.429
she feared the most?

00:07:11.429 --> 00:07:16.699
Now, 40 years after the night that reshaped
her life, the nightmare she dreaded so much

00:07:16.699 --> 00:07:21.509
— the one she tried so hard to prevent — finally
came true.

00:07:21.509 --> 00:07:26.520
Laurie is pretty much down for the count and
recovering during most of "Halloween Kills"

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:30.639
and she's not around for the big showdown,
so when word of Karen's death reaches her

00:07:30.639 --> 00:07:35.469
ears in the next movie, we may perhaps see
the most unhinged version of the character

00:07:35.469 --> 00:07:36.469
yet.

00:07:37.469 --> 00:07:40.580
And then there's Allyson, who seems to be
living out a fate not too different from her

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:46.809
grandmother — the Halloween curse now has
infected a new generation of the Strode family.

00:07:46.809 --> 00:07:51.409
She has now lost two parents in the same night
at the hands of Michael Myers.

00:07:51.409 --> 00:07:55.909
The question is, will she spiral down a dark
path similar to that of Laurie?

00:07:55.909 --> 00:08:00.620
Or perhaps she'll be stricken with a terrible
guilt in addition to all that grief.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:04.619
After all, she did disobey Karen, who implored
her to stay at the hospital.

00:08:04.619 --> 00:08:06.669
"The police are out there looking for him.

00:08:06.669 --> 00:08:09.459
You think you're going to be the one to find
him?"

00:08:09.459 --> 00:08:14.050
Instead of sitting tight and staying safe,
she became obsessed with settling a score

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:17.729
and allowed herself to get swept up in the
whole mob mentality.

00:08:17.729 --> 00:08:22.969
Had she stayed at the hospital, her mother
would still, most likely, be alive.

00:08:22.969 --> 00:08:25.619
As for Michael, how could he have survived?

00:08:25.619 --> 00:08:31.110
In this new trilogy, you have people describing
him as evil incarnate or saying things like

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:36.550
"The more he kills, the more he transcends,"
but the source of his unnatural abilities

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:38.229
has yet to be explained.

00:08:38.229 --> 00:08:43.209
"A man couldn't have survived that fire."

00:08:43.209 --> 00:08:48.440
No human would be able to withstand the pulverizing
inflicted on him during the "Halloween Kills''

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:49.440
finale.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:50.440
Is he superhuman?

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:52.790
Or maybe even something supernatural?

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:57.810
So far, it hasn't been addressed in David
Gordon Green's saga, but we may find out next

00:08:57.810 --> 00:09:01.899
year when the trilogy wraps up with "Halloween
Ends."

